0,"input":3016,"out":1751},{"k":60,"t":13,"read":197248,"write":0,"input":357,"out":794},{"k":61,"t":13,"read":198272,"write":0,"input":1746,"out":361},{"k":62,"t":13,"read":200192,"write":0,"input":1035,"out":40},{"k":63,"t":13,"read":201088,"write":0,"input":362,"out":142},{"k":64,"t":14,"read":201472,"write":0,"input":162,"out":238},{"k":65,"t":14,"read":201728,"write":0,"input":1835,"out":231},{"k":66,"t":14,"read":203648,"write":0,"input":505,"out":560}],"judgment":{"met":5,"total":5,"criteria":[{"id":"forward_database","behavior":"A custom Prefetch queryset for a forward ForeignKey with no explicit database uses the parent instance’s database through the existing router, including correct related data when default and other contain different rows.","essential":true},{"id":"reverse_database","behavior":"The same parent-database behavior holds for a reverse OneToOneField custom Prefetch queryset with no explicit database.","essential":true},{"id":"explicit_database","behavior":"An explicit database selected on the custom queryset with using() continues to take precedence; the fix does not force all custom querysets onto the parent database.","essential":true},{"id":"router_hints","behavior":"Existing router behavior and instance hints are preserved, with routing performed at the appropriate point rather than prematurely fixing the default database.","essential":true},{"id":"prefetch_compatibility","behavior":"Existing queryset reuse, cached-relation handling, empty-prefetch behavior and unaffected many-to-many paths retain their observable behavior; the patch does not bypass prefetching or add unnecessary per-object database queries.","essential":true}],"verdicts":[{"id":"forward_database","verdict":"met","evidence":"ForwardManyToOneDescriptor.get_prefetch_querysets() adds `queryset._add_hints(instance=instances[0])` before constructing the related lookup. This supplies the parent instance to existing database routing for custom querysets without an explicit database. The regression test exercises `Prefetch(relation, queryset=queryset)` for `relation=\"house\"` across `for db in (\"other\", \"default\", \"other\")`, checking related names against `[f\"{related_db} house {pk}\" for pk in (1, 2)]`."},{"id":"reverse_database","verdict":"met","evidence":"ReverseOneToOneDescriptor.get_prefetch_querysets() likewise adds `queryset._add_hints(instance=instances[0])`. Existing routing therefore receives the parent instance for custom reverse-one-to-one querysets. The same database-content assertions cover `relation=\"main_room_of\"` through `for relation in (\"house\", \"main_room_of\")`."},{"id":"explicit_database","verdict":"met","evidence":"The implementation adds hints with `queryset._add_hints(instance=instances[0])` without assigning a database or calling `.using()`, preserving the existing explicit-database contract. The regression test constructs `queryset = House.objects.using(db)`, calls `self.assertPrefetchDatabase(prefetch, parent_db, db)` across different parent databases, and asserts `self.assertEqual(queryset._db, db)`. Its router raises `AssertionError(\"Unexpected read routing\")` if explicit selection incorrectly invokes routing."},{"id":"router_hints","verdict":"met","evidence":"Both changes use `queryset._add_hints(instance=instances[0])`, which updates hints without resolving or fixing a database prematurely. Existing routing and other hints remain applicable. The test creates a queryset with `hints={\"custom_hint\": \"value\"}`, verifies `router.db_for_read.assert_not_called()` before evaluation, and checks `self.assertEqual(hints[\"custom_hint\"], \"value\")` and `self.assertIs(hints.get(\"instance\"), rooms[0])`. It exercises both router abstention and an explicit router choice with `for router_db in (None, \"default\")`."},{"id":"prefetch_compatibility","verdict":"met","evidence":"The only production changes are the two `_add_hints()` calls; existing prefetch filtering, cache population, cloning, and many-to-many paths remain intact. Regression assertions cover queryset reuse (`self.assertIsNone(queryset._db)`), evaluated-cache preservation (`self.assertIs(list(queryset)[0], cached_house)`), cached relations (`self.assertIs(getattr(rooms[0], relation), cached_house)`), and empty inputs (`prefetch_related_objects([], prefetch)`). Query-count assertions use `self.assertNumQueries(query_databases.count(\"default\"), using=\"default\")` and the corresponding `\"other\"` assertion, requiring only parent and related queries, followed by zero-query checks for related-object access."}],"pass":true},"outcome":"5/5 criteria met","results":[{"c":1045,"at":2,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":19162,"at":3,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":22222,"at":4,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":21779,"at":5,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":21300,"at":6,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":19652,"at":7,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":23470,"at":8,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":4878,"at":9,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":20583,"at":11,"t":2,"cut":null},{"c":20171,"at":12,"t":2,"cut":null},{"c":20233,"at":13,"t":2,"cut":null},{"c":12291,"at":14,"t":2,"cut":null},{"c":3693,"at":15,"t":2,"cut":null},{"c":13431,"at":17,"t":3,"cut":null},{"c":19120,"at":18,"t":3,"cut":null},{"c":24597,"at":19,"t":3,"cut":null},{"c":18558,"at":21,"t":4,"cut":null},{"c":19727,"at":22,"t":4,"cut":null},{"c":20323,"at":23,"t":4,"cut":null},{"c":20886,"at":24,"t":4,"cut":null},{"c":26367,"at":25,"t":4,"cut":null},{"c":6321,"at":26,"t":4,"cut":null},{"c":9620,"at":28,"t":5,"cut":null},{"c":25043,"at":29,"t":5,"cut":null},{"c":31226,"at":30,"t":5,"cut":null},{"c":25992,"at":31,"t":5,"cut":null},{"c":11141,"at":33,"t":6,"cut":null},{"c":9133,"at":34,"t":6,"cut":null},{"c":575,"at":35,"t":6,"cut":null},{"c":4268,"at":36,"t":6,"cut":null},{"c":4478,"at":37,"t":6,"cut":null},{"c":721,"at":39,"t":7,"cut":null},{"c":4259,"at":41,"t":8,"cut":null},{"c":575,"at":42,"t":8,"cut":null},{"c":40149,"at":44,"t":9,"cut":null},{"c":9429,"at":45,"t":9,"cut":null},{"c":14743,"at":47,"t":10,"cut":null},{"c":6512,"at":49,