sing() continues to take precedence; the fix does not force all custom querysets onto the parent database.","essential":true},{"id":"router_hints","behavior":"Existing router behavior and instance hints are preserved, with routing performed at the appropriate point rather than prematurely fixing the default database.","essential":true},{"id":"prefetch_compatibility","behavior":"Existing queryset reuse, cached-relation handling, empty-prefetch behavior and unaffected many-to-many paths retain their observable behavior; the patch does not bypass prefetching or add unnecessary per-object database queries.","essential":true}],"verdicts":[{"id":"forward_database","verdict":"met","evidence":"ForwardManyToOneDescriptor now executes `queryset = querysets[0]` followed by `queryset._add_hints(instance=instances[0])`. This supplies the parent instance to existing database routing, whose fallback uses the instance’s database. The regression test creates matching keys with different database contents and checks `[getattr(room, to_attr or relation).name for room in rooms]` against `[f\"other house {pk}\" for pk in (1, 2)]`."},{"id":"reverse_database","verdict":"met","evidence":"ReverseOneToOneDescriptor likewise adds `queryset._add_hints(instance=instances[0])` immediately after selecting the custom queryset. Existing routing therefore receives the parent instance for this path too. Tests exercise `for relation in (\"house\", \"main_room_of\")` and verify related objects have `house._state.db == \"other\"`."},{"id":"explicit_database","verdict":"met","evidence":"The implementation only calls `queryset._add_hints(instance=instances[0])`; it does not assign `_db` or replace the queryset’s database selection. Existing `using()` precedence remains intact. The explicit-selection test uses `queryset = House.objects.using(database)` with a router returning the opposite database, then checks `router.db_for_read.assert_not_called()` and `self.assertEqual(queryset._db, database)`."},{"id":"router_hints","verdict":"met","evidence":"Both changed paths use `_add_hints(instance=instances[0])`, preserving existing hints through the helper’s update contract and leaving database resolution to existing routing. Neither change evaluates `queryset.db` nor fixes a database with `using()`. Coverage initializes `House.objects.db_manager(hints={\"custom\": True}).all()` and checks router arguments equal `{\"custom\": True, \"instance\": rooms[0]}`."},{"id":"prefetch_compatibility","verdict":"met","evidence":"The only executable changes are the two `_add_hints(instance=instances[0])` calls; filtering, evaluation, relation caching, and many-to-many paths remain unchanged. These calls perform no database queries. Reuse coverage checks `self.assertIsNone(queryset._db)`, `self.assertIsNone(queryset._result_cache)`, and `self.assertFalse(queryset.query.where)`. Cached and empty input coverage invokes `prefetch_related_objects(rooms, prefetch)` and `prefetch_related_objects([], prefetch)` under zero-query assertions. Partial-cache coverage requires one related query and checks `self.assertIs(getattr(rooms[0], relation), cached_house)`."}],"pass":true},"outcome":"5/5 criteria met","results":[{"c":196,"at":2,"t":1,"cut":48},{"c":10156,"at":3,"t":1,"cut":48},{"c":8974,"at":4,"t":1,"cut":48},{"c":10261,"at":5,"t":1,"cut":48},{"c":11926,"at":6,"t":1,"cut":48},{"c":10951,"at":7,"t":1,"cut":48},{"c":10796,"at":8,"t":1,"cut":48},{"c":10871,"at":9,"t":1,"cut":48},{"c":10394,"at":10,"t":1,"cut":48},{"c":10269,"at":11,"t":1,"cut":48},{"c":9350,"at":12,"t":1,"cut":48},{"c":11237,"at":13,"t":1,"cut":48},{"c":12196,"at":14,"t":1,"cut":48},{"c":1190,"at":15,"t":1,"cut":48},{"c":10344,"at":17,"t":2,"cut":48},{"c":11156,"at":18,"t":2,"cut":48},{"c":9835,"at":19,"t":2,"cut":48},{"c":10948,"at":20,"t":2,"cut":48},{"c":10658,"at":21,"t":2,"cut":48},{"c":10523,"at":22,"t":2,"cut":48},{"c":9517,"at":23,"t":2,"cut":48},{"c":2410,"at":24,"t":2,"cut":48},{"c":2359,"at":25,"t":2,"cut":48},{"c":20